    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d221">

                <pb facs="0336" n="266" sameAs="frus:frus1862/pg266"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Stuart.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1862-07-01"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >July</hi> 1, 1862.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> In acknowledging the receipt of Lord
                    Lyons’s note of the 12th ultimo, touching the cases of British subjects,
                    prisoners of war, who may have been forced against their will into the service
                    of the enemy of the United States, he was informed by this department that the
                    attention of the Secretary of War had been invited to the subject. I now have
                    the honor to enclose to you a copy of that officer’s reply.</p>
                <p>I avail myself of this opportunity to offer to you, sir, the assurance of my high
                    consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>F. W. SEWARD, <hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                    Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William Stuart, </hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d221-a1.xml" xpointer="d221-a1"/>
            </div>
